      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.6885939240455627,
      "reading_order": 6,
      "text": "3. IC and per acids of chlorine are $\\mathrm{HClO}_3$ and\n$\\mathrm{HClO}_4$, respectively.\n$\\therefore$ The formulae of salts with trivalent metal\nare $\\mathrm{M}(\\mathrm{ClO}_3)_3$ and $\\mathrm{M}(\\mathrm{ClO}_4)_3$. The number of\noxygen atoms in these salts, respectively, are 9\nand 12."
    },
    {
