      "text": "4. Carbon forms two oxides CO and $\\mathrm{CO}_2$, and the\nvalencies of carbon are 2 and 4, respectively.\n$\\mathrm{CO}_2 + \\mathrm{H}_2\\mathrm{O} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{H}_2\\mathrm{CO}_3$ carbonic acid\n$\\mathrm{NaOH} + \\mathrm{H}_2\\mathrm{CO}_3 \\rightarrow \\mathrm{NaHCO}_3$ (or) $\\mathrm{Na}_2\\mathrm{CO}_3$\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260317_fac1ab83-81e6-422f-84cf-3b23b86ae39a_6_block_008",
      "coordinates": {
