        "y2": 2315.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.8111689686775208,
      "reading_order": 9,
      "text": "5. Both Pb and Sn form two oxides $\\text{PbO}$, $\\text{PbO}_2$\nand $\\text{SnO}$, $\\text{SnO}_2$, respectively. In $\\text{PbO}$ and $\\text{SnO}$,\nthe valencies of Pb and Sn are two, and in\n$\\text{PbO}_2$ and $\\text{SnO}_2$ the valencies of Pb and Sn are\nfour."
    },
    {
