      "text": "6. A can form $\\mathrm{A}^+$ ion and B can form $\\mathrm{B}^{+2}$ ion.\nC can form $\\mathrm{C}^{+3}$ ion and D can form $\\mathrm{D}^{+4}$ or $\\mathrm{D}^{+6}$\nion.\n$\\therefore$ P is $\\mathrm{A}_2\\mathrm{O}$, Q is BO, R is $\\mathrm{C}_2\\mathrm{O}_3$, and S is $\\mathrm{DO}_2$ or\n$\\mathrm{DO}_3$.\nHence, the correct option is (a)."
