      "text": "10. Metal with electronic configuration 2, 8, 14, 2 is\nFe. Fe can form two hydroxides $\\text{Fe(OH)}_2$ and\n$\\text{Fe(OH)}_3$. The formulae of salts of these hydrox-\nides with sulphuric acid are $\\text{FeSO}_4$ and $\\text{Fe}_2(\\text{SO}_4)_3$.\n\n$$ \\text{Fe(OH)}_2 + \\text{H}_2\\text{SO}_4 \\rightarrow \\text{FeSO}_4 + \\text{H}_2\\text{O} $$\n$$ \\text{Fe(OH)}_3 + 3\\text{H}_2\\text{SO}_4 \\rightarrow \\text{Fe}_2(\\text{SO}_4)_3 + 3\\text{H}_2\\text{O} $$\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
